From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ams: Kiln's IFS settings in the filament system settings

With Kiln OS's IFS driver, the filament system settings (device
operations) get the IFS's own rows:

- Endless Spool: Colour match (Exact, Similar, Any colour;
  IFS_AUTO_REFILL MATCH=). The on/off switch is the panel's own
  Endless Spool switch (0038).
- Setup: Tool to slot (Slot per file, Auto colour; IFS_MAP_MODE MODE=).
- Calibration: Tune IFS (IFS_TUNE; greyed while it runs or the IFS is
  busy, refused during a print), its progress and message while it
  runs, the last result after, and the tuned feed speed, load distance
  per slot and unload distance ("Not tuned" where the defaults apply).
- Filament Feeder: Pre-feed slot 1-4 (IFS_PREFEED CHANNEL=n), greyed
  for an empty slot, the loaded slot or a busy IFS, refused during a
  print.

The driver's version is the system version shown at the top. Each
section shows only where the driver publishes its fields; nothing
changes on other firmware.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
